 sentence of ten mutually exclusive events, expressed as a logarithm to base 10.", "source": "UNECE_REC20", "source_version": "GitHub datasets/unece-units-of-measure (Redistributed)"}, {"canonical_code": "UNECE_REC20_Q16", "standard_code": "Q16", "name": "natural unit of information", "symbol": "nat", "category": "3.6", "source_status": "", "status": "ACTIVE", "description": "Logarithmic unit for information equal to the content of decision of a sentence of ,718 281 828 459 mutually exclusive events, expressed as a logarithm to base Euler value e.", "source": "UNECE_REC20", "source_version": "GitHub datasets/unece-units-of-measure (Redistributed)"}, {"canonical_code": "UNECE_REC20_Q17", "standard_code": "Q17", "name": "shannon per second", "symbol": "Sh/s", "category": "3.6", "source_status": "", "status": "ACTIVE", "description": "Time related logarithmic unit for information equal to the content of decision of a sentence of two mutually exclusive events, expressed as a logarithm to base 2.", "source": "UNECE_REC20", "source_version": "GitHub datasets/unece-units-of-measure (Redistributed)"}, {"canonical_code": "UNECE_REC20_Q18", "standard_code": "Q18", "name": "hartley per second", "symbol": "Hart/s", "category": "3.6", "source_status": "", "status": "ACTIVE", "description": "Time related logarithmic unit for information equal to the content of decision of a sentence of ten mutually exclusive events, expressed as a logarithm to base 10.", "source": "UNECE_REC20", "source_version": "GitHub datasets/unece-units-of-measure (Redistributed)"}, {"canonical_code": "UNECE_REC20_Q19", "standard_code": "Q19", "name": "natural unit of information per second", "symbol": "nat/s", "category": "3.6", "source_status": "", "status": "ACTIVE", "description": "Time related logarithmic unit for information equal to the content of decision of a sentence of 2,718 281 828 459 mutually exclusive events, expressed as a logarithm to base of the Euler value e.", "source": "UNECE_REC20", "source_version": "GitHub datasets/unece-units-of-measure (Redistributed)"}, {"canonical_code": "UNECE_REC20_Q20", "standard_code": "Q20", "name": "second per kilogramm", "symbol": "s/kg", "category": "3.5", "source_status": "", "status": "ACTIVE", "description": "Unit of the Einstein transition probability for spontaneous or inducing emissions and absorption according to ISO 80000-7:2008, expressed as SI base unit second divided by the SI base unit kilogram.", "source": "UNECE_REC20", "source_version": "GitHub datasets/unece-units-of-measure (Redistributed)"}, {"canonical_code": "UNECE_REC20_Q21", "standard_code": "Q21", "name": "watt square metre", "symbol": "W\u00b7m\u00b2", "category": "3.5", "source_status": "", "status": "ACTIVE", "description": "Unit of the first radiation constants c1 = 2\u00b7p\u00b7h\u00b7c0\u00b2, the value of which is 3,741 771 18\u00b710?\u00b96-fold   that of the comparative value of the product of the derived SI unit watt multiplied with the power of the SI base unit metre with the exponent 2.", "source": "UNECE_REC20", "source_version": "GitHub datasets/unece-units-of-measure (Redistributed)"}, {"canonical_code": "UNECE_REC20_Q22", "standard_code": "Q22", "name": "second per radian cubic metre", "symbol": "1/(Hz\u00b7rad\u00b7m\u00b3)", "category": "3.5", "source_status": "", "status": "ACTIVE", "description": "Unit of the density of states as an expression of angular frequency as complement of the product of hertz and radiant and the power of SI base unit metre by exponent 3 .", "source": "UNECE_REC20", "source_version": "GitHub datasets/unece-units-of-measure (Redistributed)"}, {"canonical_code": "UNECE_REC20_Q23", "standard_code": "Q23", "name": "weber to the power minus one", "symbol": "1/Wb", "category": "3.5", "source_status": "", "status": "ACTIVE", "description": "Complement of the derived SI unit weber as unit of the Josephson constant, which value is equal to the 384 597,891-fold of the reference value gigahertz divided by volt.", "source": "UNECE_REC20", "source_version": "GitHub datasets/unece-units-of-measure (Redistributed)"}, {"canonical_code": "UNECE_REC20_Q24", "standard_code": "Q24", "name": "reciprocal inch", "symbol": "1/in", "category": "3.5", "source_status": "", "status": "ACTIVE", "description": "Complement of the unit inch according to the Anglo-American and Imperial system of units.", "source": "UNECE_REC20", "source_version": "GitHub datasets/unece-units-of-measure (Redistributed)"}, {"canonical_code": "UNECE_REC20_Q25", "standard_code": "Q25", "name": "dioptre", "symbol": "dpt", "category": "3.5", "source_status": "", "status": "ACTIVE", "description": "Unit used at the statement of relative refractive indexes of optical systems as complement of the focal length with correspondence to: 1 dpt = 1/m.", "source": "UNECE_REC20", "source_version": "GitHub datasets/unece-units-of-measure (Redistributed)"}, {"canonical_code": "UNECE_REC20_Q26", "standard_code": "Q26", "name": "one per one", "symbol": "1/1", "category": "3.5", "source_status": "", "status": "ACTIVE", "description": "Value of the quotient from two physical units of the same kind as a numerator and denominator whereas the units are shortened mutually.", "source": "UNECE_REC20", "source_version": "GitHub datasets/unece-units-of-measure (Redistributed)"}, {"canonical_code": "UNECE_REC20_Q27", "standard_code": "Q27", "name": "newton metre per metre", "symbol": "N\u00b7m/m\u00b2", "category": "3.5", "source_status": "", "status": "ACTIVE", "description": "Unit for length-related rotational moment as product of the derived SI unit newton and the SI base unit metre divided by the SI base unit metre.", "source": "UNECE_REC20", "source_version": "GitHub datasets/unece-units-of-measure (Redistributed)"}, {"canonical_code": "UNECE_REC20_Q28", "standard_code": "Q28", "name": "kilogram per square metre pascal second", "symbol": "kg/(m\u00b2\u00b7Pa\u00b7s)", "category": "3.5", "source_status": "", "status": "ACTIVE", "description": "Unit for the ability of a material to allow the transition of steam.", "source": "UNECE_REC20", "source_version": "GitHub datasets/unece-units-of-measure (Redistributed)"}, {"canonical_code": "UNECE_REC20_Q29", "standard_code": "Q29", "name": "microgram per hectogram", "symbol": "\u00b5g/hg", "category": "1S", "source_status": "", "status": "ACTIVE", "description": "Microgram per hectogram.", "source": "UNECE_REC20", "source_version": "GitHub datasets/unece-units-of-measure (Redistributed)"}, {"canonical_code": "UNECE_REC20_Q30", "standard_code": "Q30", "name": "pH (potential of Hydrogen)", "symbol": "pH", "category": "2", "source_status": "", "status": "ACTIVE", "description": "The activity of the (solvated) hydrogen ion (a logarithmic measure used to state the acidity or alkalinity of a chemical solution).", "source": "UNECE_REC20", "source_version": "GitHub datasets/unece-units-of-measure (Redistributed)"}, {"canonical_code": "UNECE_REC20_Q31", "standard_code": "Q31", "name": "kilojoule per gram", "symbol": "kJ/g", "category": "1S", "source_status": "", "status": "ACTIVE", "description": "", "source": "UNECE_REC20", "source_version": "GitHub datasets/unece-units-of-measure (Redistributed)"}, {"canonical_code": "UNECE_REC20_Q32", "standard_code": "Q32", "name": "femtolitre", "symbol": "fl", "category": "1S", "source_status": "", "status": "ACTIVE", "description": "", "source": "UNECE_REC20", "source_version": "GitHub datasets/unece-units-of-measure (Redistributed)"}, {"canonical_code": "UNECE_REC20_Q33", "standard_code": "Q33", "name": "picolitre", "symbol": "pl", "category": "1S", "source_status": "", "status": "ACTIVE", "description": "", "source": "UNECE_REC20", "source_version": "GitHub datasets/unece-units-of-measure (Redistributed)"}, {"canonical_code": "UNECE_REC20_Q34", "standard_code": "Q34", "name": "nanolitre", "symbol": "nl", "category": "1S", "source_status": "", "status": "ACTIVE", "description": "", "source": "UNECE_REC20", "source_version"